--TEST--
A keyed `foreach` over a `Core\ObjectMap<tainted string, int>` binds its key as `tainted string`, so a plain `string` key does not compile while `var` and a written `tainted string` do — `rule:iteration/keyed-interfaces`, `rule:security/taint-propagation`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:iteration/keys-and-values-from-a-map
Core\ObjectMap<tainted string, int> $hits = new Core\ObjectMap<tainted string, int>();

// The keys are tainted, so a plain `string` key does not compile.
foreach ($hits as string $page => int $n) {
}

// `var` takes the key type, so `$path` is `tainted string`. This compiles.
foreach ($hits as var $path => int $m) {
    echo $path, "\n";
}

// A key written as `tainted string` also compiles.
foreach ($hits as tainted string $url => int $k) {
    echo $url, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0851]: this key can come from outside the program, so it must be `tainted string`
  --> case.nvs:6:19
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
